**Password Generation Function in PHP**
======================================

The following PHP function generates a random password based on user-defined criteria and ensures it meets common security standards.

### Function Code

```php
/**
 * Generates a random password based on user-defined criteria.
 *
 * @param int  $length              The length of the password.
 * @param bool $includeUppercase    Whether to include uppercase letters.
 * @param bool $includeNumbers      Whether to include numbers.
 * @param bool $includeSpecialChars Whether to include special characters.
 *
 * @return string The generated password.
 */
function generatePassword(int $length = 12, bool $includeUppercase = true, bool $includeNumbers = true, bool $includeSpecialChars = true): string
{
    // Define the character sets to use
    $charSets = [
        'lowercase' => 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz',
    ];

    if ($includeUppercase) {
        $charSets['uppercase'] = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';
    }

    if ($includeNumbers) {
        $charSets['numbers'] = '0123456789';
    }

    if ($includeSpecialChars) {
        $charSets['specialChars'] = '!@#$%^&*()_+-={}:<>?,./';
    }

    // Ensure at least one character from each set is included
    $password = [];
    foreach ($charSets as $charSet) {
        $password[] = $charSet[random_int(0, strlen($charSet) - 1)];
    }

    // Fill the rest of the password with random characters from all sets
    $allChars = implode('', $charSets);
    for ($i = count($password); $i < $length; $i++) {
        $password[] = $allChars[random_int(0, strlen($allChars) - 1)];
    }

    // Shuffle the password to avoid the first characters always being from the same set
    shuffle($password);

    return implode('', $password);
}

// Example usage:
$password = generatePassword(16, true, true, true);
echo "Generated Password: $password\n";
```

